  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment history includes positive values (e.g., >0.00), indicating bullish bias that often overestimates prices.",
    "Reduce forecast magnitude by 5-10% if recent true outcomes show mean reversion toward lower levels after a spike.",
    "Increase forecast lag by 1-2 days if model overreacts to recent price spikes (e.g., overshoots after 65+ peaks).",
    "Apply upward bias correction if true outcomes consistently exceed model forecasts during low sentiment periods (e.g., sentiment=0.00 and price rises >5% from prior day).",
    "Use a smoothing filter (e.g., 3-day moving average) to dampen short-term volatility in forecasts when sentiment is neutral or negative."
  ]
}
